{title: Into All The Truth}
{subtitle: John 16:13}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [Fsus4] [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I still have much to [Eb]tell you
[Gm]But you [F]cannot bear it [Eb]now
[Gm]The path is long and [F]wide
I am going to [Eb]the Father [Bb]now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the Spirit of [F/A]truth comes
[Gm]He will guide you gen[Eb]tly
[Gm]He will not speak on his [F]own
But speak whatever he [Eb]hears
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He will declare [F]to you
[Gm]The things that are [Eb]coming
[Bb]Into all the truth [F]he leads
And your [Eb]heart is humming
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]He will glorify [F/A]me
[Gm]Taking what is mine to [Eb]speak
[Gm]All that the Father [F]has
Is given to us to [Eb]keep
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]A little while and you [F]will lose sight
And a[Bb]gain a little [Eb]while
[Gm]You will see me in the [F]light
[Eb]No longer hidden from the [Bb][F]night
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]Into all the truth [Eb]he guides
The Spirit of [Bb]truth
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Gm7] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
